<title>BRAZIL: Brazil petrochemical firm EDN to be auctioned.</title>
<headline>Brazil petrochemical firm EDN to be auctioned.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Development Bank (BNDES) is selling off a minority stake in petrochemical firm Estireno do Nordeste (EDN) today on the Rio de Janeiro stock exchange (BVRJ).</p>
<p>The bank is auctioning 26.74 percent of EDN's total capital belonging to Petroquisa, a subsidiary of state oil firm Petrobras, for a minimum price of 17 million reais ($17 million) or 36 reais per lots of 1,000 shares.</p>
<p>-- Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151</p>
</text>
